  "reasoning": "The defendant cut down 39 poplar trees without obtaining the required forestry administrative approval or a logging permit. This constitutes illegal logging. Since the trees were privately owned (purchased from an individual) and not collective or state-owned, the specific charge of '盗伐林木' does not apply. According to the correction rule, the statutory offense name should be listed without the character “罪”. Therefore, the appropriate charge is '非法采伐林木'.",
  "final_answer": "[罪名]非法采伐林木<eoa>"
